(synth/play sound {note :c4 velocity 0.8 seconds nil}) "Plays sound, or a sample, at :note and :velocity, held :seconds or until synth/release, and returns its voice. In oxmacs only, as are the other functions that play."
(synth/release voice) "Lets go of voice, so its envelope's release and its echoes ring out."
(synth/stop (voice)) "Stops voice at once, or without one everything that plays: voices and the song."
(synth/loop song) "Plays song again and again. Looping another song while one plays swaps it in at the next bar, keeping the bar count, the voices still ringing and the effects of tracks with the same name and effects, so code can be changed while it plays."
(synth/set control value) "Sets the control called control, such as :cutoff, to value; every sound using it hears the change smoothly."
(synth/controls) "The controls sounds have used, as maps of :name, :value, :default, :low, :high and :automated, true while an automation moves it."
(synth/automate control points) "Moves control bar by bar along points, as [[0 400] [8 2000]], counting bars from when the song started looping, taking over from the song's own automation of it; nil points stop it."
(synth/position) "A map of the looping song's :bar, counted from 0 with its fraction, and :tempo, or nil when no song plays."
(synth/scope (count)) "The last moments of what plays as count numbers from -1 to 1, 256 unless given, for drawing its wave."
(synth/level) "How loud what plays is now, from 0 to 1."
